&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alpaca is a US-headquartered, global leader in agent-first brokerage infrastructure&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;for stocks, ETFs, options, crypto, fixed income, 24/5 trading, and more.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Amongst our subsidiaries, Alpaca is a licensed financial services company, serving hundreds of financial institutions across 40 countries with our institutional-grade APIs. This includes broker-dealers, investment advisors, wealth managers, hedge funds, and crypto exchanges, totalling over 10 million brokerage accounts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our global team is a diverse group of experienced engineers, traders, and brokerage professionals who are working to achieve our mission of opening financial services to everyone on the planet. We&#39;re deeply committed to open-source contributions and fostering a vibrant community, continuously enhancing our award-winning, developer-friendly API and the robust infrastructure behind it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alpaca is proudly backed by $400 million in funding from top-tier global investors including Portage Ventures, Spark Capital, Tribe Capital, Social Leverage, Horizons Ventures, Opera Tech Ventures, SBI Group, Derayah Financial, Unbound, Peak XV, Elefund, and Y Combinator.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Team Members:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a dynamic team of 400+ globally distributed members who thrive working from our favorite places around the world, with teammates spanning the USA, Canada, Japan, Hungary, Nigeria, Brazil, the UK, and beyond!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re searching for passionate individuals eager to contribute to Alpaca&#39;s rapid growth. If you align with our core values—Stay Curious, Have Empathy, and Be Accountable—and are ready to make a significant impact, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Alpaca is building the infrastructure layer that partners across Europe use to launch and scale brokerage products. We&#39;re expanding our EU footprint - with growing market access, a regional roadmap, and ambitions across equities, ETFs, derivatives, direct connectivity, securities lending, tax reporting, and tax-wrapper products. We&#39;re hiring a Product Manager to own that expansion end-to-end: define the strategy, ship the products, and work with regulators, partners, and internal teams to make Alpaca the brokerage platform of choice across the EU.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re seeking a Product Manager to define and drive new product initiatives and manage a portfolio of existing products across EU markets. With a deep understanding of the regional regulatory landscape, including MiFID II / MiFIR, ESMA, CSDR, national competent-authority frameworks, and member-state tax and tax-wrapper regimes, you will shape the product strategy that enables Alpaca to scale its brokerage infrastructure across the EU.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is equal parts strategy and delivery. You&#39;ll decide what we build versus buy, how we sequence the region’s roadmap, and which partnerships and connectivity paths get us there - and then ship the brokerage features, tax-wrapper functionality, integrations, and operational workflows that partners and institutional clients depend on every day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What You&#39;ll Walk Into&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You won&#39;t be starting from zero. You&#39;ll be owning live problems:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EU market access: scaling from initial access to full product coverage while meeting MiFID II / MiFIR, ESMA, and local NCA requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The rest of the EU roadmap: prioritizing and delivering the next wave of brokerage capabilities across equities, ETFs, and regional market needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EU direct connectivity: building and owning connectivity to EU venues and market infrastructure, reducing reliance on intermediary paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EU broker partnerships: evaluating, onboarding, and integrating local brokers to expand coverage and resilience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-border complexity: passporting, multi-jurisdiction onboarding, and coordinating between Alpaca&#39;s global platform and EU market infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tax and tax wrappers: building tax-wrapper account functionality (e.g. PEA / PEA-PME, ISK, PIR) and the tax surface underneath it - tax lots / cost basis, dividend withholding, WHT reclaim, and country-specific tax reporting - so partners can offer jurisdiction-specific wrappers on Alpaca, not just a generic brokerage account.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Things You Get To Do&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own brokerage products tailored for EU markets, including equities, ETFs, tax-wrapper accounts, and related regional offerings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the EU tax and tax-wrapper product surface end-to-end: wrapper eligibility and contribution rules, tax-lot / cost-basis tracking, withholding and reclaim, and the local reporting files partners and end-users need to stay compliant.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive brokerage product strategy by analyzing ROI, regional market competition, regulatory requirements, and build-vs-buy scenarios.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and execute the product roadmap with a focus on MiFID II / MiFIR-compliant features and regional market needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write product requirements and work with engineers to execute programs that meet local regulatory and market standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve brokerage operation efficiency by providing solutions and owning the metrics, with a focus on regional settlement, custody, and clearing workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead customer calls around brokerage process and product issues to gain insights and translate them into product improvements for EU clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report timely and accurately on product status and results to internal and external stakeholders, including regional partners and institutional clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with local operations teams to ensure seamless integration between Alpaca&#39;s global platform and EU market infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Who You Are (Must-Haves)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excited about what Alpaca is building and passionate about expanding financial infrastructure across the EU.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in computer science, engineering, finance, or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in Product Management, Engineering, Consulting, and/or starting a startup, preferably within financial services or fintech.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated interest and experience in brokerage, capital markets, or fintech within the EU.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of MiFID II / MiFIR, ESMA, the EU capital markets landscape, and how member-state tax and tax-wrapper rules shape product design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills in English, both written and verbal, with excellent collaboration abilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business acumen to understand tradeoffs between stakeholders and technology feasibility with time and budget constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Who You Might Be (Nice-to-Haves)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience and background working on and developing brokerage products in EU markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical background working with APIs, particularly in financial services or trading platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with CSDR, EMIR, T2S, or CSD connectivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience shipping tax-wrapper or tax-reporting products (e.g. PEA / PEA-PME, ISK, PIR), including tax lots, withholding, and local reporting files.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with cross-border / passporting investment products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional EU language(s) beyond English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working at a fintech, startup, or EU-authorized investment firm.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Take Care of You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Competitive Salary &amp;amp; Stock Options&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Health Benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;New Hire Home-Office Setup: One-time USD $500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Monthly Stipend: USD $150 per month via a Brex Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Alpaca is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace dedicated to pursuing and hiring a diverse workforce.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
